  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q22-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "22",
    "prompt": "Let $b\\ne1$ be a positive number.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q22-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Suppose that\n$$a_1,a_2,a_3,\\ldots$$\nis a geometric sequence of positive terms. Show that\n$$\\log_b a_1,\\log_b a_2,\\log_b a_3,\\ldots$$\nis an arithmetic sequence.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The common difference is $\\log_b r$, where $r>0$ is the original common ratio.\n\nUse the logarithm quotient law on consecutive terms.",
          "worked": "Let the common ratio be $r>0$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}&=r\\\\\\log_b a_{n+1}-\\log_b a_n&=\\log_b\\left(\\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}\\right)\\\\\\log_b a_{n+1}-\\log_b a_n&=\\log_b r.\\end{align*}$$\nThe difference between consecutive logarithms is constant, so the sequence is arithmetic.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q22-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Suppose that\n$$a_1,a_2,a_3,\\ldots$$\nis an arithmetic sequence. Show that\n$$b^{a_1},b^{a_2},b^{a_3},\\ldots$$\nis a geometric sequence.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The common ratio is $b^d$, where $d$ is the original common difference.\n\nUse the exponent quotient law on consecutive terms.",
          "worked": "Let the common difference be $d$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}a_{n+1}-a_n&=d\\\\\\frac{b^{a_{n+1}}}{b^{a_n}}&=b^{a_{n+1}-a_n}\\\\\\frac{b^{a_{n+1}}}{b^{a_n}}&=b^d.\\end{align*}$$\nThe ratio between consecutive terms is constant, so the sequence is geometric.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
